Third-party software in the Docker image
----------------------------------------

The published image (ghcr.io/xantiagoma/casatube) is a combined distribution.
This file and LICENSE are in it at /usr/share/licenses/casatube/. CasaTube's
own code is MIT; the image also contains, unmodified:

yt-dlp (release binary yt-dlp_musllinux / yt-dlp_musllinux_aarch64)
  https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
  yt-dlp's source is released under the Unlicense, but the release binaries
  bundle code under other licences and, as a combined work, are licensed under
  the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later. The exact release is in the
  image tag and in the label io.casatube.ytdlp.version; its source and its
  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt are on that release's GitHub page:
  https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases

FFmpeg, x264 and the other Alpine Linux packages
  https://ffmpeg.org, https://www.videolan.org/developers/x264.html
  Installed from the Alpine Linux package repositories. FFmpeg as built by
  Alpine is licensed GPL-2.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later; x264 is
  GPL-2.0-or-later. Every package's name, version and licence can be listed
  from inside the image with:
    docker run --rm --entrypoint apk ghcr.io/xantiagoma/casatube list -I
  The corresponding source code for every Alpine package, including the build
  recipe used, is published by Alpine Linux at https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports
  (the branch matching the image's Alpine release, see ALPINE_VERSION in the
  Dockerfile) and https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/.

  Some codecs FFmpeg supports (H.264, HEVC, AAC and others) may be covered by
  patents in some countries. Whether a licence is needed for your use is your
  responsibility.

Bun
  https://bun.sh, MIT License. Bun statically links JavaScriptCore (WebKit,
  LGPL-2.1 / BSD) and other components listed at
  https://bun.sh/docs/project/license

JavaScript dependencies
  Installed from npm into /app/node_modules, each with its own licence file
  there. The direct dependencies are MIT, Apache-2.0 or ISC licensed;
  package.json lists them.

The source code for anything in the image that requires it is available at the
locations above. If you cannot obtain it there, open an issue in this
repository and it will be provided.


